  <CaseSection id="process" title="How it was built">
    <CaseProse>
      <p>
        Routes, params, form field names, and HTMX targets stayed exactly the same, so the
        pipeline and every integration were untouched.
      </p>
      <p>
        Interfaces drift when nothing stops them, so the style guide lives in
        the app, renders every component live with the code to copy, and states its own rules:
        where the system lives, how it changes, and what checks it has to pass.
      </p>
      <p>
        It also has a section for AI coding agents. The team builds with them, so the same rules
        sit in the repo’s agent instructions too. An agent asked to
        build a page reads the system before it writes a class.
      </p>
    </CaseProse>

